# ~/.config/based/shareable-deny.txt — the per-machine half of the shareable
# deny list (the tracked half is config/shareable-deny.txt). One token per
# line, `#` comments. Machine identity goes HERE, not in the tracked file:
# a tracked deny list publishes the exact strings it exists to protect.
#
# Prefix a line with `word:` to match only as a whole word — a short token
# without it matches inside every longer string and denies half the tree.
#
# Examples (shapes only — put your real values, then delete these lines):
#   my-machine-name
#   my-tailnet-name
#   word:myhandle
